# Build context for the core image.
#
# The repository-wide .dockerignore is written for the fetch zone, which is
# deliberately given as little as possible — no migrations, no config, no web
# assets, because an image that does not contain them cannot be talked into
# using them (D-11, V-3).
#
# The core image is the opposite case: it runs migrations, verifies evidence
# against the shipped TSA certificates, and serves the console. BuildKit uses
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to .dockerignore, so the two images
# get the context each should have without either one loosening the other.

.venv/
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.import_linter_cache/

# T2 and T3 (docs/REPO_POLICY.md). Never in an image, for the same reason they
# are never in the T1 repository.
docs/
phases/
.claude/
spikes/
*.env
.env
